# Physics budget

A full physical character `Human` or `Bird` is about 16 `Rigidbody2D`,
muscles, and a 200 Hz step. This is the hero budget: keep 1–2 such
characters on screen at once, not a crowd.

- Leave the player at 200 Hz. Switching to 50 Hz breaks the controller
  and is not a way to raise FPS.
- `humanCount` 10–50 is allowed only as a laboratory load in
  `SampleScene`, not as the `World` game mode.
- In the `World` game `treeCount` stays 0 (grove is `TreeRig.Static`).
  The yard may hold a small Flock, hens, and a few leftover dogs.
  Off-camera NPCs rest (`NpcRest`): Kinematic, no 200 Hz drive.
  The hero Human stays at 200 Hz. Watch flight in scene `Bird`, the
  tree in scene `Tree`. Do not plant `Sway` in World.
- In the game, `Physics2D jobs` may be on. `HeadlessTrial` must turn
  them off: one-leg probe `oneg_r` determinism depends on it.
- Keep `Maximum Allowed Timestep` low, about 0.05 s, not 0.333 s,
  so a dropped frame does not queue a long physics-step backlog.
- `OverlapBoxAll` in `FixedUpdate` is forbidden: use `NonAlloc`.
  Do not call `Find` or `GetComponent` every step — cache the references.
- `CollisionDetectionMode2D.Continuous` is needed on the feet, not on
  every segment. Do not turn `Interpolate` off for FPS: physics runs at
  200 Hz, the frame is about 60 Hz.
- A 10 s stand measurement is skewed by exe startup. Estimate the budget
  from a 30 s run or from the difference between runs of different
  duration.
- Do not change `lumbarP`, muscles, or other control gains for
  performance: that changes body stability, not the cost of the model.

# Course (college 28.08)

The game is one controlled `Human` with honest muscle physics, not a
crowd of active ragdolls and not a platformer with an upward force.
Do not stop the model. Do not lower 200 Hz: the `World` profile is
already taken (below); there is no new controller. 50 Hz is closed by
the stand. A controller substep on coarser physics is not a saving.
Do not amputate the arms: they are in the CoM and the stance. Do not
fuse the pelvis with the chest. Merging `Muscle`+`JointFriction` into
one pass is legitimate plumbing after the profile. 100 Hz
(`-fixedDelta 0.01`) is a separate experiment with no other edits, not
the next step. The bottleneck is the main thread and 3–4 steps per
frame, not "all cores busy".

